WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.202
Module nine:

2
00:00:01.202 --> 00:00:01.984
strategies.

3
00:00:01.984 --> 00:00:06.316
Holding and buying in parts, trend following, mean reversion,

4
00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:10.862
grids and neutral strategies, and the hidden assumption of each.

5
00:00:11.862 --> 00:00:14.355
A strategy is easy to describe in rules.

6
00:00:14.355 --> 00:00:15.914
It is more useful to ask:

7
00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:19.342
what has to happen to the price for this to make money?

8
00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:21.212
That is the hidden assumption.

9
00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:25.326
Every strategy has one, even one that calls itself market-neutral.

10
00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.269
Buy and hold has a single assumption:

11
00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:31.974
in years the price will be higher.

12
00:00:31.974 --> 00:00:36.269
Buying in parts is often sold as a way to buy cheaper,

13
00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.974
but it only smears the entry date.

14
00:00:38.974 --> 00:00:44.224
Starting in 2019, 2020 or 2023, buying at once gave twice as much.

15
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:47.326
Starting in 2018 or 2022, the opposite.

16
00:00:48.326 --> 00:00:49.491
Trend following:

17
00:00:49.491 --> 00:00:54.150
be in the market while the price rises, and leave when it falls.

18
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.242
The assumption:

19
00:00:55.242 --> 00:00:58.081
strong moves last longer than it seems.

20
00:00:58.081 --> 00:01:03.832
On bitcoin since 2017, the 200-day average rule grew seven times against 17 for

21
00:01:03.832 --> 00:01:08.054
holding, but its worst drawdown was 64 percent against 83.

22
00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:10.133
Mean reversion:

23
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.657
buy after a sharp fall and sell after the bounce.

24
00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:14.735
The assumption:

25
00:01:14.735 --> 00:01:16.533
sharp moves are overdone.

26
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:20.489
The result is many small profits and rare large losses,

27
00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:22.862
when the fall turns into a crash.

28
00:01:22.862 --> 00:01:27.608
On bitcoin since 2017, growth of two times against 17 for holding:

29
00:01:27.608 --> 00:01:29.766
crypto trends for a long time.

30
00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:35.190
A grid bot places buy orders below the price and sell orders above it.

31
00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:38.665
Each pass of the price down and back is a small profit.

32
00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:39.613
The assumption:

33
00:01:39.613 --> 00:01:41.825
the price will move within a range.

34
00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:46.691
If it goes down and does not come back, the grid keeps buying a falling coin.

35
00:01:46.691 --> 00:01:49.029
And with a step of a quarter percent,

36
00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:52.126
fees eat about 80 percent of each round's profit.

37
00:01:53.126 --> 00:01:53.494
Carry:

38
00:01:53.494 --> 00:01:56.007
buy the coin and sell a perpetual future,

39
00:01:56.007 --> 00:02:01.035
collecting funding; the assumption is that funding stays positive and the exchange

40
00:02:01.035 --> 00:02:01.954
stays reliable.

41
00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:06.920
Market making earns the spread as long as it exceeds the losses from trading with

42
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.147
those who know more.

43
00:02:08.147 --> 00:02:12.806
Stat arbitrage expects diverged coins to converge faster than fees eat them.

44
00:02:13.806 --> 00:02:19.015
Each strategy in the lesson has a button that opens work mode with the idea already

45
00:02:19.015 --> 00:02:19.580
selected.

46
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.525
There you can test it honestly:

47
00:02:21.525 --> 00:02:24.726
with fees, on different coins and on held-out data.

48
00:02:25.726 --> 00:02:26.723
The main points.

49
00:02:26.723 --> 00:02:31.147
Every strategy has a hidden assumption about price, and if it is wrong,

50
00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:33.079
the mechanics will not save it.

51
00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:38.188
In a rising market, strategies that leave the market more often lose to holding on

52
00:02:38.188 --> 00:02:38.624
return.

53
00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:42.550
And neutral strategies lose to fees and to those who know more.
